WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:08.425
♪♪

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:11.303
Justin:
The first director really gets
to put the stamp on the thing.

00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:14.973
And then the other directors
have the difficult job of

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:19.144
essentially singing the same
song, but in different keys.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:21.313
Justin:
Each one has been completely
unique.

00:00:21.313 --> 00:00:23.190
We've had 3 woman directors on
this show

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.942
Logan:
and that has been so fun.

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.110
Logan:
I haven't worked with so many
women in my life.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:32.032
We're wrapping this season with
Clare Kilner who's just one of
the best directors.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.994
She has a really specific
vision, but she lets you get
there in your own freedom.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.538
We're not going to the adventure
place.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.958
♪♪

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.626
We're finding Charlie and going
home. 

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:44.086
♪♪

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:45.087
What about dad?

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:45.754
♪♪

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:49.841
Melissa:
In the episode 1 there is this
beautiful moment between Margo and Allie.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:54.763
Where he says to Margot "I
have this idea to build a boat."

00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:55.722
A boat?

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.557
♪♪

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.058
Sure.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:58.976
♪♪

00:00:58.976 --> 00:01:00.310
[SMIRK]
-Why not?

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.687
♪♪

00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:03.855
Look, no no I I was thinking
about a barge.

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.357
Upside- plenty of space. 

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:07.234
Downside- kinda ties you into
one place. 

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.736
The end shot of season 1,
they're on that boat.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.281
Melissa:
When the guy got exactly what he
planned to do. 

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:16.451
Melissa:
He managed to get Margot on that
boat.

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:18.704
And now she's going nowhere but
with him.

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.916
Neil:
I think the single most
important take away from episode 7 

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.670
is Allie's face in the final
shot. 

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.464
Neil:
There's a kinda ferocity to his
joy.

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:36.054
-(Crying)
-Neil: There's also the first
real indication of a latent madness.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:37.681
Justin:
I don't know what his end game
is.

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:39.433
But I alway get to a sense of
foreboding

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:41.351
cause I think how far up river
can you go

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:42.686
before it can go very dark.

00:01:42.686 --> 00:01:44.688
(Crying)
-Dad?
-Stop.

00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:47.399
It's incredible the power of
family.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:51.403
Melissa:
When you see them no matter what
they get put through.

00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:52.863
Melissa:
They will say to the kids,

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:55.532
Melissa:
it's not usually like this, but
we made it right?

00:01:55.532 --> 00:02:00.203
That optimism brainwashes the
kids to thinking what they just
saw was really not so bad.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.496
Allie:
Pretty good, right?

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:03.665
Mexican s'mores.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:04.291
They're really good, dad.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.709
Allie:
umm.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:09.421
Neil:
They will never live a life
that's typical 

00:02:09.421 --> 00:02:12.132
for a north American middle
class white family.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.343
Neil:
But are they defined by that
Americanness?

00:02:14.343 --> 00:02:17.304
Neil:
Is that formative psychological 
and cultural experience

00:02:17.304 --> 00:02:18.764
Neil:
something which can be escaped.

00:02:19.181 --> 00:02:21.391
There's no America.
There's just us.

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:23.185
We just don't throw that away.

00:02:23.185 --> 00:02:23.977
♪♪

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.355
Neil:
Season 1 is a travel narrative.

00:02:26.355 --> 00:02:30.442
Neil:
But all travelers must at some
point reach their destination.

00:02:30.442 --> 00:02:33.653
Neil:
The next journey is about the
destination.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.989
Neil:
And be careful what you wish
for.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.368
Neil:
There's a great line by Horace
which is,

00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:44.122
"They change the sky but not
their souls who cross the sea".

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:47.626
Neil:
And if there is a theme to this
show, that's it. 

00:02:47.626 --> 00:02:50.587
What did I tell you? 
It's perfect.

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.381
(Laughing)

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:56.968
♪♪

